.TH BINMAN 1 "2026-08-02" "BinMan 1.9.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
binman \- install and manage personal command-line tools
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B binman
.RI [ global-options ]
.RI command
.RI [ arguments ]
.br
.B binman install
.RI target
.RI [ install-options ]
.br
.B binman test
.RI name
.RI [ \-\- args ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
BinMan installs single-file scripts, multi-file application directories, and
remote scripts as commands. It provides user or system installation targets,
app shims, entry-point detection, Python virtual environments, backups,
rollback snapshots, manifests, a terminal UI, Docker/Podman management, and
a collection of bundled utility scripts.
.PP
The default user command directory is
.IR ~/.local/bin .
The default user app store is
.IR ~/.local/share/binman/apps .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B install TARGET
Install one file, directory, or HTTP(S) URL. A file becomes a command with its
last extension removed. A directory is stored as an app and exposed through a
shim.
.TP
.B scripts
Browse and install scripts from the cached BinMan repository.
.TP
.B uninstall NAME [NAME...]
Remove installed commands or apps. Use \fB--dry-run\fR to preview removal.
.TP
.B verify
Verify installed command executability and app payload, entry, and shim paths.
.TP
.B list
List installed commands. With \fBfzf\fR available, use the interactive
browser and previews.
.TP
.B update TARGET
Reinstall a target with overwrite enabled. \fB--from\fR updates executable
files in a directory.
.TP
.B doctor [APP]
Report environment state and optionally prepare Python app environments.
\fB--all\fR checks every installed app; \fB--fix-path\fR patches common shell
startup files.
.TP
.B docker [ACTION] [APP]
Manage BinMan Docker/Podman containers. Actions include \fBup\fR, \fBdown\fR,
\fBrestart\fR, \fBlogs\fR, \fBfollow\fR, \fBshell\fR, \fBedit\fR, \fBbuild\fR,
\fBremove\fR, \fBnuke\fR, \fBpurge\fR, \fBprune\fR, \fBorphans\fR, and
\fBrun\fR.
.TP
.B new NAME
Create a language-specific single-file or app scaffold. Options include
\fB--app\fR, \fB--lang\fR, \fB--dir\fR, and \fB--venv\fR.
.TP
.B wizard
Run the interactive project, manifest, Git, optional GitHub, install, and
container scaffolding workflow.
.TP
.B backup [FILE]
Archive BinMan-curated app directories and their matching shims. Virtual
environments are included by default. With no arguments in a TTY, the guided
flow asks which apps to include, whether to keep virtual environments, and
where to write the archive before showing a confirmation summary. Use
\fB--exclude-venvs\fR for a lean archive; unrelated files in the user's
\fB~/.local/bin\fR are not included.
.TP
.B restore FILE
Merge a ZIP, tar.gz, or tgz archive into the active target directories. In a
TTY the command opens the archive picker.
.TP
.B self-update
Clone the configured BinMan repository, validate the source, refresh the
source cache, and reinstall the running command.
.TP
.B rollback
Apply the latest automatic rollback snapshot.
.TP
.B prune-rollbacks
Remove rollback snapshots beyond \fBBINMAN_ROLLBACK_KEEP\fR.
.TP
.B analyze
Report filesystem, directory, and large-file usage without deleting anything.
.TP
.B bundle [FILE]
Export installed curated apps, matching shims, and a manifest into an archive.
.TP
.B test NAME [-- ARGS]
Run an installed command with \fB--help\fR, or with explicit arguments after
\fB--\fR. \fBtest stress\fR runs the temporary-fixture stress harness.
.TP
.B sudo NAME [ARGS...]
Run an installed command through \fBsudo\fR.
.SH INSTALL OPTIONS
.TP
.B --from DIR
Install executable regular files directly inside DIR. The scan is not
recursive.
.TP
.B --manifest FILE
Install a line manifest, or a JSON array when \fBjq\fR is available.
.TP
.B --entry COMMAND
Set the app command explicitly, for example \fBpython3 src/main.py\fR.
.TP
.B --workdir DIR, --cwd DIR
Change to a directory inside the stored app before running its entry.
.TP
.B --venv
Use an app-local Python virtual environment.
.TP
.B --req FILE
Use a named requirements file for app venv setup.
.TP
.B --python BIN
Choose the Python interpreter used to bootstrap a venv.
.TP
.B --name NAME
Override the installed command or shim name.
.TP
.B --link
Store a directory app as a symlink for development. Ordinary single files are
still copied.
.TP
.B --force
Overwrite an existing target.
.TP
.B --system
Use /usr/local/bin and /usr/local/share/binman/apps; sudo may be used.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B --quiet
Reduce output.
.TP
.B --no-clear
Do not clear the terminal in interactive views.
.TP
.B --reindex
Rebuild the inventory cache before dispatching the command.
.TP
.B --engine docker|podman
Prefer a container engine for Docker actions.
.TP
.B --version
Print the BinMan version.
.TP
.B --help
Print command help.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/bin
User-installed command files and app shims.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/binman/apps
User-installed app payloads.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/binman/source
Cached repository used by \fBbinman scripts\fR.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/binman
Inventory cache and BinMan state.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/binman/rollback
Automatic snapshots when \fBBINMAN_AUTO_BACKUP=1\fR is enabled.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/binman/docker
Container metadata; override with \fBBINMAN_DOCKER_DIR\fR.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BINMAN_AUTO_BACKUP=1
Enable pre-change rollback snapshots. Disabled by default.
.TP
.B BINMAN_ROLLBACK_KEEP=N
Keep N rollback snapshots; the default is 20.
.TP
.B BINMAN_SOURCE_DIR=DIR
Override the cached repository source directory.
.TP
.B BINMAN_REPO_URL=URL
Override the repository cloned by self-update.
.TP
.B BINMAN_DOCKER_DIR=DIR
Override Docker/Podman metadata storage.
.TP
.B BINMAN_DEBUG=1
Enable verbose inventory and manifest diagnostics.
.TP
.B BINMAN_NO_CLEAR=1
Disable terminal clearing in interactive views.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
binman install ./tool.sh
binman install ./MyApp --entry 'python3 src/main.py' --venv
binman install --manifest tools.txt
binman list
binman doctor --fix-path
binman backup tools.zip
binman restore tools.zip
BINMAN_AUTO_BACKUP=1 binman update ./tool.sh
binman test tool -- --help
.fi
.SH SAFETY
BinMan does not sandbox installed scripts. Bundled scripts may invoke sudo,
mount, package managers, firewall tools, SSH, GitHub CLI, Docker, or remote
installers. Review scripts before running them with elevated privileges.
.PP
Automatic rollback snapshots are opt-in. Archives are local, unencrypted
copies and may contain executable code and host/path metadata.
.PP
A BinMan child process cannot mutate its parent shell's command hash table. On
install and uninstall BinMan refreshes its own process and prints the suitable
parent-shell command, usually \fBrehash\fR for Zsh or \fBhash -r\fR for Bash.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bash (1),
.BR fzf (1),
.BR git (1),
.BR rsync (1)
.SH BUGS
Report bugs and implementation mismatches at the BinMan repository:
.IR https://github.com/karialo/binman .
